  "definition": {
    "id": "ACT-COMPOSE",
    "instanceId": "EX-CORE-U3-20-required-composition",
    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Write a practical message",
    "subtitle": "A tradeoff in the budget · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare costs, benefits and constraints before making a practical decision.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-20-required-composition-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Compose a purposeful message",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-20-required-composition-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "written",
            "prompt": "A tradeoff in the budget · 1: Write a practical explanation for someone joining the situation late. State the problem, a supported reason or constraint, and a clear proposed next step.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "我想买一个相机，朋友和我去商店。店里的相机很漂亮，比我想买的贵很多。卖东西的人说可以用信用卡，让我先拿回家用。\n\n我有点儿想买，觉得今天不用拿出那么多钱，好像就不贵了。朋友问我最后要花多少，用信用卡也一样，买相机的钱都要给。\n\n我再看要多少钱，发现自己这个月还要买课本，也要坐车去看妈妈。我不能用这些钱买太贵的相机，就请卖东西的人拿便宜一点儿的给我看。\n\n我试了那个便宜一点儿的相机，虽然没有那么大，照相也可以，最后用银行卡买了它。朋友说，先看自己需要什么和要花多少钱，再想怎么给钱。\n\n回家以后，我把相机拿给妈妈看，告诉她还有坐车的钱。卡是给钱的办法，不是说东西便宜了。我喜欢这个能用、也买得起的相机。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Write your own message",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed writing practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "The problem, constraint and next step connect coherently."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I distinguished the source facts from my proposal."
              }
            ],
            "minLength": 1
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
    ],
